   "item": {
    "subject_key": "biology",
    "unit_number": 1,
    "topic_code": "1.1",
    "topic_title": "Structure of Water and Hydrogen Bonding",
    "stem": "When sweat evaporates from a person's skin, the skin cools. Which explanation correctly connects water's molecular structure to this biological effect?",
    "choices": [
     {
      "choice_key": "A",
      "choice_text": "Water's polarity produces covalent bonds between neighboring water molecules; breaking these bonds during evaporation absorbs energy from the skin, cooling it.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "The trap is confusing bonds within molecules with attractions between molecules: neighboring water molecules form hydrogen bonds, not covalent bonds. Evaporation separates water molecules without breaking their covalent H–O bonds. Fix: Identify whether the bond connects atoms within one water molecule or connects two different water molecules."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "B",
      "choice_text": "Water's polarity enables hydrogen bonds between water molecules; breaking these bonds during evaporation releases energy, and this energy release removes heat from the skin.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "The trap is reversing the energy change of bond breaking: overcoming hydrogen bonds requires energy rather than releasing it. Cooling occurs because evaporation absorbs heat from the skin. Fix: Check whether your explanation makes separation of attracted molecules require energy input or release energy."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "C",
      "choice_text": "Water's polarity enables hydrogen bonds between water molecules; these give water high specific heat capacity, meaning evaporation requires little energy and therefore cools the skin.",
      "is_correct": false,
      "rationale": "The trap is confusing specific heat capacity with heat of vaporization. High specific heat capacity limits temperature change as water absorbs heat; water's high heat of vaporization means evaporation requires substantial energy. Fix: Ask whether the observation involves changing liquid water's temperature or changing liquid water into vapor, then select the matching property."
     },
     {
      "choice_key": "D",
      "choice_text": "Water's polarity enables hydrogen bonds between water molecules; overcoming these attractions during evaporation requires energy absorbed from the skin, cooling it.",
      "is_correct": true,
      "rationale": "This explanation connects polarity to hydrogen bonding and then to evaporative cooling. Energy is required to separate hydrogen-bonded water molecules during evaporation, so evaporating sweat absorbs heat from the skin."
     }
    ]
   },
